From: Lume Retro OS
Subject: [PATCH] command: GET_STATUS reports the video frame counter

The network command GET_STATUS tells the system, core and content of the
running game. The reply now also carries the video frame counter as a last
field, ",frames=<n>". r36os-logd asks for the status on every metrics sample
and computes the game FPS as the counter difference over the time difference,
so the metrics show whether each core keeps full speed on the console.

The field comes after ",crc32=", so a parser that cuts the content name at
",crc32=" keeps working.

--- a/command.c
+++ b/command.c
@@ -1060,8 +1060,12 @@
       _len    += strlcpy(reply + _len, ",", sizeof(reply) - _len);
       _len    += strlcpy(reply + _len,
             path_basename(path_get(RARCH_PATH_BASENAME)), sizeof(reply) - _len);
+      /* Lume: the video frame counter lets a monitor compute the game FPS
+       * (difference between two replies over their time difference). It
+       * comes last so parsers that cut at ",crc32=" keep working. */
       _len    += snprintf(reply + _len, sizeof(reply) - _len,
-            ",crc32=%lx\n", (unsigned long)content_get_crc());
+            ",crc32=%lx,frames=%llu\n", (unsigned long)content_get_crc(),
+            (unsigned long long)video_state_get_ptr()->frame_count);
    }
    else
        _len = strlcpy(reply, "GET_STATUS CONTENTLESS", sizeof(reply));
